L263 -- the real-mass phantom pincer: the equivalence principle versus the Oort limit

====================================================================================================
A. a uniform external field is unobservable to a real fluid (the hydrostatic identity)
====================================================================================================
  [PASS] A1 the hydrostatic equation in the freely falling frame equals the lab-frame equation with the uniform field removed (identity, all components)
           (a real fluid's equilibrium around a star depends on the star's field and the tidal field only; |g_ext| does not enter)
    tidal acceleration across 1 pc from the Galaxy ~ 5.7e-14 m/s^2; the Sun's own field at 1 pc = 1.4e-13 m/s^2 (ratio 0.41)

====================================================================================================
B. the uncapped deep-MOND phantom of a point mass: M_ph(<r) = M (r/r_M - 1)
====================================================================================================
  [PASS] B1 M_dyn(<r) = M r/r_M and M_ph = M (r/r_M - 1) follow from g = sqrt(G M a0)/r (identity: symbolic ratio 1 and three numeric points to 1e-9)
           (ratio = 1)
    canonical: r_M(Sun) = 7960 AU = 0.0386 pc; M_ph(<1 pc) = 24.9 M_sun; Jacobi radius 1.40 pc -> M_ph(<r_J) = 35.2 M_sun
    alt: r_M(Sun) = 7252 AU = 0.0352 pc; M_ph(<1 pc) = 27.4 M_sun; Jacobi radius 1.40 pc -> M_ph(<r_J) = 38.8 M_sun
  [PASS] B2 an uncapped solar phantom carries more than 10 M_sun inside the Sun's own tidal radius on both footings

====================================================================================================
C. every star carries one: the implied local dark density versus the Oort limit
====================================================================================================
    canonical: a 0.5 M_sun star: r_M = 5628 AU; cut radius min(r_J = 1.11 pc, half-separation = 1.08 pc) = 1.08 pc; M_ph(<cut) = 19.2 M_sun; rho_dark = n_* M_ph = 1.92 M_sun/pc^3 vs the Oort dark budget 0.01-0.015 (128x)
    alt: a 0.5 M_sun star: r_M = 5128 AU; cut radius min(r_J = 1.11 pc, half-separation = 1.08 pc) = 1.08 pc; M_ph(<cut) = 21.2 M_sun; rho_dark = n_* M_ph = 2.12 M_sun/pc^3 vs the Oort dark budget 0.01-0.015 (141x)
  [FAIL] C1 the SEP-respecting real-mass phantom implies a local dark density within the Oort-limit dark budget (factor < 3) on either footing
           (factors [128, 141]x over the budget: the uncapped halos of ordinary stars are excluded by the vertical dynamics of the solar neighbourhood. [FAIL is the finding])

====================================================================================================
D. the dichotomy: capped by |g_ext| (SEP-violating field response, L243) or real mass (Oort-dead)
====================================================================================================
    G086: the sector is 'ORDINARY MATTER (p = 0)' -> True;  SOLAR_FACE_CLOSEOUT: the solar phantom is 'EFE-capped' by the Galactic field -> True;  L243: the field-response quadrupole = 6.44x the Cassini ceiling
  [FAIL] D1 the record's two properties of the phantom -- real mass (PPN = GR by the SEP) and capped by |g_ext| (the SEP violated) -- are held by the same object
           (both held: a real fluid cannot be capped by a uniform field (A1), and an uncapped real halo fails the Oort limit (C1); a cappable phantom is a field response and carries L243's quadrupole. NO THIRD READING. [FAIL is the finding])

====================================================================================================
E. correction: Milgrom's deep-MOND virial RAISES the a0 a dispersion system needs (x 81/16 = 5.06); it does not lower it
====================================================================================================
    Fornax dSph (sigma 11.7 km/s, M_b 2e7): required a0 -- framework conversion 0.30 x a0_DE; deep-MOND virial 1.53 x a0_DE (ratio 5.06)
    Coma (sigma 1000 km/s, M_b 2e14): required a0 -- framework conversion 1.61 x a0_DE; deep-MOND virial 8.15 x a0_DE (ratio 5.06)
  [PASS] E1 the deep-MOND virial coefficient multiplies the required a0 by 81/16 = 5.0625 exactly (so the 09-17 flag's direction was wrong)
           (Fornax at 0.3 x a0_DE (framework) -> 1.5 x (Milgrom): the isolated deep virial puts Fornax near the line; Coma 1.6 -> 8.1 x (the known MOND cluster deficit, ~2.8 in mass))
  [FAIL] E2 under BOTH conventions a single a0 places Fornax and Coma on one line within a factor 2
           (no: the dispersion channels are not on one line under either conversion; the per-object Jeans treatment (FIFTY item 3, IDEAS_100 item 1) is required. [FAIL is the finding])

L263 COMPLETE: 4/7 checks PASS.  VERDICT: the real-mass reading of the phantom is closed by the equivalence principle and the Oort
limit (a real fluid cannot be capped by a uniform field; uncapped, every star carries ~20 M_sun inside its tidal radius, 100x the local dark
budget); the cappable reading is the field response L243 kills.  The two readings the record splices are each dead on its own.
